## Architecture Review

When asked to review architecture:

- Read all module directories and build config files to map module boundaries.
- Identify the declared architecture pattern from README or inline comments.
- Trace imports in each layer — check that dependency direction flows presentation → domain → data only.
- Flag any reversal: domain importing data, data importing presentation.
- Detect circular dependencies between modules.
- Flag god modules: more than 3 unrelated responsibilities or imported by every other module.
- Check DI wiring files for bindings placed in the wrong layer.
- Flag tight coupling: swapping a module would require changes in unrelated modules.
- Flag low cohesion: module mixes concerns that belong in separate units.
- Order all findings P0 (critical) → P3 (minor) with file and line references.
